---
const swatches = [
	'oklch(0.82 0.10 235)',
	'oklch(0.78 0.13 255)',
	'oklch(0.74 0.15 270)',
	'oklch(0.78 0.15 210)',
	'oklch(0.82 0.15 175)',
	'oklch(0.86 0.14 152)',
];
---

<section id="craft" class="relative border-t border-line py-24 sm:py-32">
	<div class="container-x">
		<div class="reveal grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr_1fr] lg:items-end">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">The craft</p>
				<h2 class="display mt-5 text-[clamp(2.4rem,5.4vw,4.4rem)]">
					This site is <span class="serif-accent text-gradient">the demo.</span>
				</h2>
			</div>
			<p class="max-w-lg text-lg leading-relaxed text-body lg:justify-self-end">
				Everything you’re looking at was designed and hand-coded with current web platform features. Here’s what’s running on this page right now.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="mt-16 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
			<article class="spotlight card reveal overflow-hidden p-7">
				<div class="relative h-28 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line [background:radial-gradient(80%_120%_at_20%_0%,oklch(0.55_0.16_270/0.7),transparent_60%),radial-gradient(70%_100%_at_90%_40%,oklch(0.65_0.12_220/0.55),transparent_60%),radial-gradient(60%_90%_at_50%_120%,oklch(0.7_0.13_152/0.45),transparent_60%)]" aria-hidden="true"></div>
				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold">WebGL shader</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">The aurora behind the hero is a hand-written GPU fragment shader. It reacts to your cursor and pauses when it’s off-screen.</p>
			</article>

			<article class="spotlight card reveal p-7">
				<div class="flex h-28 flex-col justify-center gap-3 rounded-xl border border-line bg-night px-5" aria-hidden="true">
					<div class="h-1.5 overflow-hidden rounded-full bg-white/[0.06]"><div class="craft-progress h-full origin-left rounded-full bg-gradient-to-r from-sky via-accent to-leaf"></div></div>
					<div class="h-1.5 w-2/3 overflow-hidden rounded-full bg-white/[0.06]"><div class="craft-progress h-full origin-left rounded-full bg-white/40"></div></div>
				</div>
				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold">Scroll-driven animation</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">Reveals, the 3D showcase, and these bars run on CSS scroll timelines. No animation library, no scroll listeners.</p>
			</article>

			<article class="spotlight card reveal p-7">
				<div class="flex h-28 items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-line bg-night">
					<button type="button" data-open-palette class="btn-ghost !py-2.5 !text-sm">
						Try it: <kbd class="font-mono">⌘K</kbd> / <kbd class="font-mono">Ctrl K</kbd>
					</button>
				</div>
				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold">Command palette</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">The kind of keyboard-first UI you’d find in the best software products — fully accessible, on every page of this site.</p>
			</article>

			<article class="spotlight card reveal p-7">
				<div class="glow-border flex h-28 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-night" aria-hidden="true">
					<span class="font-mono text-xs text-muted">@property --border-angle</span>
				</div>
				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold">Houdini CSS properties</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">Registered custom properties let CSS animate things it normally can’t, like this rotating gradient border.</p>
			</article>

			<article class="spotlight card reveal p-7">
				<div class="flex h-28 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line" aria-hidden="true">
					{swatches.map((c) => <div class="flex-1" style={`background:${c}`}></div>)}
				</div>
				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold">OKLCH color</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">The palette is defined in OKLCH, a perceptually even color space, so gradients stay vivid instead of turning muddy.</p>
			</article>

			<article class="spotlight card reveal p-7">
				<div class="flex h-28 items-center justify-center gap-3 rounded-xl border border-line bg-night font-mono text-xs" aria-hidden="true">
					<span class="rounded-md border border-line px-2.5 py-1.5 text-muted">/</span>
					<span class="text-gradient text-base">→</span>
					<span class="rounded-md border border-line-strong px-2.5 py-1.5 text-ink">/work</span>
				</div>
				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold">View transitions</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">Moving between pages cross-fades natively in the browser, like an app, with zero JavaScript. Try opening <a href="/work" class="link-arrow">the work</a>.</p>
			</article>
		</div>

		<p class="reveal mt-10 text-center font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-muted">
			Also: pre-rendered HTML · JavaScript only for interactive islands · hover the cards for the cursor spotlight
		</p>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	@supports (animation-timeline: view()) {
		.craft-progress {
			animation: grow linear both;
			animation-timeline: view();
			animation-range: entry 20% cover 55%;
		}
	}
	@keyframes grow {
		from { transform: scaleX(0.04); }
		to { transform: scaleX(1); }
	}
</style>

<script>
	import { OPEN_PALETTE_EVENT } from '../lib/events';
	document.querySelectorAll('[data-open-palette]').forEach((b) =>
		b.addEventListener('click', () => window.dispatchEvent(new Event(OPEN_PALETTE_EVENT)))
	);
</script>
